    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, my neighbor just installed this massive automated hydroponic setup right next to my bedroom window. it runs these misting cycles every couple hours and there's this really heavy, sweet scent coming from it that makes me feel super lightheaded and anxious whenever it's active. i'm worried about what kind of airborne particulates or chemical compounds might be in that mist. what are some ways i can neutralize or filter those out so they don't get into my house?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your reaction suggests you should immediately stop sharing the air with the system by sealing your bedroom window and using a high-quality HEPA+activated carbon air purifier indoors. If indoor filtration isn't enough, you can temporarily install temporary storm windows to create a significant physical barrier between the mist and your living space. It is also wise to contact your landlord or building management, as indoor hydroponic systems running mist frequently can be a disturbance and may violate local nuisance or zoning laws. Finally, you should test the water source of the neighboring system to rule out potential contamination from untreated runoff before considering long-term solutions.",
